{"tool_name":"vhldb","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"vhldb","home":"http://vhldb.bio.unipd.it/","summary":"A database of interactors and mutations of the human von Hippel-Lindau tumor suppressor protein (pVHL).","addition_date":"2017-03-29T11:36:21Z","last_update_date":"2020-06-16T10:55:22Z","tool_type":["Database portal","Web API","Web application"],"version":["3.0"],"collections":["Rare Disease"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:vhldb","cost":"Free of charge (with restrictions)","credit":[{"email":"silvio.tosatto@unipd.it","name":"Silvio C.E. Tosatto","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://protein.bio.unipd.it"},{"name":"ELIXIR-ITA-PADOVA","typeEntity":"Project","typeRole":["Support"],"url":"http://elixir.bio.unipd.it/"},{"name":"University of Padua, Department of Biomedical Sciences, BioComputing UP lab","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"],"url":"http://protein.bio.unipd.it/"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://vhldb.bio.unipd.it/help"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["ELIXIR-EE"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Mutation identifier","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2538"},"format":[{"term":"Sequence feature table format (text)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2206"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Protein function analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2414"},{"term":"Query and retrieval","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0224"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Protein report","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0896"},"format":[{"term":"CSV","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3752"},{"term":"HTML","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2331"},{"term":"JSON","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3464"},{"term":"TSV","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3475"},{"term":"XML","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2332"}]}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"VHLdb","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-ITA-PADOVA","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/srep31128","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 The Author(s) 2016.Mutations in von Hippel-Lindau tumor suppressor protein (pVHL) predispose to develop tumors affecting specific target organs, such as the retina, epididymis, adrenal glands, pancreas and kidneys. Currently, more than 400 pVHL interacting proteins are either described in the literature or predicted in public databases. This data is scattered among several different sources, slowing down the comprehension of pVHL's biological role. Here we present VHLdb, a novel database collecting available interaction and mutation data on pVHL to provide novel integrated annotations. In VHLdb, pVHL interactors are organized according to two annotation levels, manual and automatic. Mutation data are easily accessible and a novel visualization tool has been implemented. A user-friendly feedback function to improve database content through community-driven curation is also provided. VHLdb presently contains 478 interactors, of which 117 have been manually curated, and 1,074 mutations. This makes it the largest available database for pVHL-related information.","authors":[{"name":"Leonardi E."},{"name":"Minervini G."},{"name":"Piovesan D."},{"name":"Quaglia F."},{"name":"Sundus F."},{"name":"Tabaro F."},{"name":"Tosatto S.C.E."}],"citationCount":13,"date":"2016-08-11T00:00:00Z","journal":"Scientific Reports","title":"VHLdb: A database of von Hippel-Lindau protein interactors and mutations"},"pmcid":"PMC4980628","pmid":"27511743","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Protein interactions","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0128"},{"term":"Protein structure analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2814"},{"term":"Rare diseases","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3325"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"VHLdb","home":"https://bio.tools/vhldb","version":"3.0","summary":"A database of interactors and mutations of the human von Hippel-Lindau tumor suppre